			"date": "2026-08-10T19:37:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> </p><p>On a related note: please use idempotent controls by default on user interfaces.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117072918305439651",
			"parentId": "117072897859595229",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117072918242071073",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T19:42:44.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@worik\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>worik</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> What do you mean?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073024482680363",
			"parentId": "117072918305439651",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik/117073023748866286",
			"author": {
				"name": "Worik",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T20:09:34.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>My Spotify player uses the same button for play and pause</p><p>It is not always 100% responsive</p><p>Did I press it properly? Better press it again, carefully, now I am paused. </p><p>If it had idempotent buttons one that does play, one that does pause, I could press the play button twice, safely, despite the platforms unavoidable poor performance </p><p>Basic UX that is mostly ignored by designers</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073043380668029",
			"parentId": "117073024482680363",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117073043032307044",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T20:14:28.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@worik\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>worik</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Sorry, are you suggesting all switches and checkboxes should also have two idempotent click targets for both states? I’m not sure I see the connection.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073057509560825",
			"parentId": "117073043380668029",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik/117073054915943841",
			"author": {
				"name": "Worik",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T20:17:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> </p><p>Not all, I am not an extremist,  on this matter</p><p>But by default a control should do the same thing if used N times in a row as it does if used once</p><p>Computer interfaces are unavoidable unreliable and idempotence really helps</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073086288369014",
			"parentId": "117073057509560825",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117073086076283141",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T20:25:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@worik\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>worik</span></a></span> I am not sure I agree with this. Separate playback and pause controls, for example, would add complexity both visually and interactively – I think in this case it would be a net negative overall.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073129964766612",
			"parentId": "117073086288369014",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik/117073128994195908",
