				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/358/626/707/396/187/original/13f15a8f67c13349.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T21:35:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> i loath switches with a passion - i always have to guess what the setting is - and always use a simple checkbox unless work forces me not to. There is no cognitive load in a checkbox.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073442895283480",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://society.oftrolls.com/@mansr/117073442847652805",
