		{
			"id": "117073639179015852",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808/117073639153776871",
			"author": {
				"name": "Curtis Wilcox",
				"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/611/015/490/799/806/original/79bff32e81a0f372.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T22:46:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>&gt; Is the toggle on when the circle is on the left or right?</p><p>When the toggle switch is 'on' and the language is left-to-right, the thumb is on the right. Whatever the language direction and writing mode, 'on' is 'end', 'off' is 'start'. This convention is true beyond Apple OSes.</p><p>What 'on' and 'off' mean depends on what it does and how it's labeled.</p><p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073666343854782",
			"parentId": "117073639179015852",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117073666171889264",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T22:52:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@cwilcox808\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cwilcox808</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> But note how the first paragraph is wholly unnecessary when explaining checkboxes the same way.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073679882983393",
			"parentId": "117073666343854782",
			"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808/117073679851754362",
			"author": {
				"name": "Curtis Wilcox",
				"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/611/015/490/799/806/original/79bff32e81a0f372.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T22:56:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> <br>True, but checkboxes are form controls and imply nothing will happen until there's a separate submit/save action. Toggle switches are meant to make something happen immediately, no second action required.<br><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073690749933232",
			"parentId": "117073679882983393",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117073688234182203",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T22:58:33.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@cwilcox808\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cwilcox808</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I don’t believe this is actually true in practice, alas – plenty of counterexamples on either side.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073813301349619",
			"parentId": "117073690749933232",
			"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808/117073813278475138",
			"author": {
				"name": "Curtis Wilcox",
				"url": "https://c.im/@cwilcox808",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/611/015/490/799/806/original/79bff32e81a0f372.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T23:30:21.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> <br>Sure, lots of examples of these conventions not being followed, on and off the web.<br>But those are the expectations set by the interfaces in the minds of users who have, consciously or unconsciously, learned these associations.<br><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073834204360395",
			"parentId": "117073813301349619",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117073834023120083",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T23:35:38.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@cwilcox808\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cwilcox808</span></a></span> I don’t think this is true, either. For as long as checkboxes have been around, there have been instant, form-less checkboxes, both on Mac OS and Windows. This isn’t even something that used to work and broke. It never worked this way. </p><p>Apple just wanted a different looking checkbox for the iPhone, and most of disambiguation between checkboxes and switches since has been wishful postrationalization that has little basis in reality.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117073835188733108",
			"parentId": "117073834204360395",
			"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary/117073834955965621",
			"author": {
				"name": "Marcin Wichary",
				"url": "https://mastodon.online/@mwichary",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/419/131/244/576/867/original/3020b744bd0ffcc4.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-10T23:35:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@cwilcox808\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cwilcox808</span></a></span> I know of many *designers* who can’t explain the difference, let alone users.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117074366851923239",
			"parentId": "117073255254511011",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik/117074366600896825",
			"author": {
				"name": "Worik",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@worik",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-11T01:51:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> Then do not do it!</p><p>Controls that are hard t use are, well, hard to use!!</p><p>I think you are arguing for anti-patterns.  I mostly experience GUIs in Web Apps and on my phone, and I find controls that change their function depending on when they are used are very disconcerting</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "117075795600352994",
			"parentId": "117073813301349619",
			"url": "https://tech.lgbt/@imsop/117075795558859584",
			"author": {
				"name": "Rowan Tommins",
				"url": "https://tech.lgbt/@imsop",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2026-08-11T07:54:28.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://c.im/@cwilcox808\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cwilcox808</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.online/@mwichary\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>mwichary</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Honestly, that supposed rule has never even occurred to me. The main place I see switches used is those deliberately hard-to-use \"privacy\" popups, where they're just form elements with a submit button.</p><p>My thought process on immediate vs on-submit is more like \"hmm, I can't see the Save button, so I guess I just close the window and hope it auto-saved\". Half the time, I load the page back up to check.</p><p>So yeah, if you're relying on that distinction being understood, please stop and just add a small flash message saying \"Saved\" when I tick a checkbox.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
	],
